 my only suggestion would be to maybe  opt for parboiled rice or  wild rice instead which are even lower  on the glycemic index and higher in  protein  so that we would see an even smaller  impact on blood sugar  all right so finally let's take a look  at exhibit c  so here we have a bean and cheese  burrito with some  roasted broccoli and plain greek yogurt  to dip  on the side now i love how simple and  easy this little lunchy lunch is  you pretty much just have to crack open  a can of beans throw it in a tortilla  with some cheese  and you're good to go i also think that  burritos in general  are another really great vehicle to use  up whatever cheap ingredients  you've got in the fridge so here we've  got protein in the beans  and the yogurt fiber rich carbs in the  tortilla and the vegetables  and of course some fat from the cheese i  also love  that this person is using plain greek  yogurt instead of sour cream for their  dip  i personally find this is such an easy  swap because  not only does it taste virtually the  same in my opinion  it's also higher in protein and calcium  compared to sour cream  while also providing some of those gut  healthy probiotic bacteria  as well i guess if i was to make any  kind of suggestion i would say that even  though  i love that we have some roasted  broccoli on the side for some veg  if you wanted to up the fiber and  antioxidants here really easily and also  add some more flavor we could easily  throw in some red onion  tomato bell pepper avocado shredded  lettuce  whatever veg is cheap wherever you are  or whatever you have handy in your  fridge  all that could go into that burrito we  could also use a whole grain tortilla  instead of  a white flour tortilla and while i am  totally a fan of refried beans i love  them  they are pretty high in sodium they  actually have about 44  of your daily needs per cup so since we  already have a good amount of salt from  the cheese  you could opt for a lower sodium canned  black beans  or pinto beans instead which would be an  even  cheaper choice okay so now that we are  all done lunches  let's take a look at dinners and we're  going to start with exhibit  a  okay so here we have a bootable kind of  thing  made with rice that's been cooked in  coconut milk  with ginger and turmeric some roasted  broccoli  that seems to be a favorite as well as  some spiced roasted chickpeas with some  lemon yogurttini sauce oh my god  that looks so bomb so we are hitting all  the  hunger crushing compounds in this meal  with some carbs from the rice  got protein from the chickpeas healthy  fats from the tahini  and some fiber-rich veg from the  broccoli i also love  how easy it is to just kind of switch up  each of these components  just depending on what you have on hand  or what you're in the mood for  so for example you could easily swap out  the chickpeas for chicken or lentils or  tofu  you could play around with the cooked or  raw veg and even mix up the carbs for  maybe some  couscous or some sweet potato or quinoa  also i love that budget friendly does  not mean  flavor free so cooking your rice with  coconut milk spices and topping it off  with a little bit of tahini  is an amazing cost-effective way to  boost flavor  of a generally really inexpensive staple  i don't have much to add other than  if you wanted to add a little bit of  crunch and some monounsaturated fats  you could add a sprinkle of some sesame  seeds  or inexpensive peanuts on top okay let's  move on to  exhibit b  [Music]  so here we have my bff shakshuka  this is an israeli dish made of eggs  some crushed tomatoes in this case it's  got some red bell pepper  onion paprika cayenne and garlic and  this person added a little bit of feta  cheese on top  for good measure okay for one i cannot  explain  to you how much i love shakshuka it is a  perfect dish for  breakfast lunch or dinner so it's the  best i also have a shikshuka recipe on  my blog which i'll link below  as well as one in the mindful glow  cookbook which i will also  link below but for me it is the ultimate  simple comfort food that relies on  really inexpensive pantry and fridge  staples  so here we're getting some fiber rich  produce from the crushed tomatoes and  bell  pepper we got protein from the eggs and  of course some fat in the cheese  this viewer also said that she enjoyed  this with some bread  to really round this out for dinner but  of course if you don't have any bread  available  you could also serve it with some rice  or quinoa  or some couscous or any grain of choice  i'm also not sure what kind of eggs are  being used here but  i do like to choose omega-3 eggs when i  can which  do offer about five times the omega-3s  of a regular egg  even though they are slightly pricier  than standard eggs that you would find  at the grocery store  this meal is so inexpensive you may be  able to  justify the cost and they're a really  great option to help sneak in some extra  omega-3s for people who  maybe don't eat a lot of fish or who are  vegetarian or vegan  also we could totally up the veg factor  here  by maybe adding in some frozen spinach  or frozen kale which is again  is a really cost-effective way to just  boost up the fiber  and the antioxidants finally let's take  a look at exhibit  c  so for our last dinner meal we have some  whole wheat pasta  topped with chickpeas cooked in a  coconut milk and  curry paste along with some bell peppers  carrots  and onions okay so does anyone else  agree that you can cook virtually  anything  in a little coconut milk and it'll  probably taste really good  like this video right now if you think  that coconut milk  is life but no honestly i do feel like  it is the ultimate inexpensive culinary  hack to  really bring simple ingredients to life  and while a can of coconut milk is  already  pretty inexpensive the powdered version  is even  cheaper so you just kind of add a little  bit of water and you have a more  flavorful  liquid for cooking things like rice or  quinoa  or for making a sauce now with that said  i love  this curry dish as an easy plant-based  meal option  i also really like the idea of using  whole wheat pasta noodles instead of the  standard rice  or kind of asian rice noodles which will  also add some extra fiber  and other micronutrients like manganese  and magnesium  we've also got some extra fiber and  protein from the chickpeas  fat from the coconut milk along some  extra fiber rich veg as well  so my bet is that this is a pretty  satiating  and also really inexpensive meal now if  we wanted to boost up the veg however  you could throw in some frozen spinach  or frozen butternut squash or when  zucchini is in season  and really cheap you could spiralize one  of those in there as well  and i also might suggest squeezing a  little bit of lime juice into the sauce  which would add some extra vitamin c to  help increase the iron absorption from  the chickpeas  that not only will add a lot of flavor  but it's also a particularly important  tip for some my plant-based friends  okay so last but not least let's move on  to snacks  so here we have a snack size yogurt bowl  made with full fat greek yogurt mixed  with a little bit of chia jam  and topped with peanut butter  strawberries granola  and some more chia jam i mean i am  definitely a fan of this snack  for the use of chia jam alone if you've  been a long time subscriber or follower  of mine  you'll know that chia jam is quite  literally my jam  but anyways if you have yet to jump on  the chia jam train  i'm gonna leave a link to my recipe down  in the description box  below it's so good um but i love making  chia jam because you can just use up any  frozen fruit or fresh  fruit that's kind of about to go bad and  it's a lot lower in sugar than  store-bought jellies or jams  plus in one tablespoon of chia seeds  there's a whopping  five grams of fiber and three grams of  protein so  it's a really cost effective way to  boost nutrition  i also love that we're using full fat  greek yogurt which has  an impressive 20 grams of protein per  cup  and also agreed on going with the higher  fat dairy option  since research does suggest that it not  only helps you feel  more satiated due to the extra fat  content but it may also possess  unique benefits for weight management  and blood sugar regulation  but generally speaking i am loving a  good yogurt bowl for a balanced snack  you know we've got protein and fat in  the yogurt and the chia seeds  and some fiber-rich carbs from the  granola and fruit i would say however  because some granolas are really high in  added sugar  if you wanted to have that crunch factor  and up the healthy fats a bit more  you could definitely add in some extra  chia hemp  flax seeds sunflower seeds inexpensive  nuts  whatever you have in your pantry or if  you want to up the fiber content  you could also add in like a little  handful of brand cereal which  is one of my favorite personal crunchy  additions to  any kind of yogurt bowl but yeah this  looks super great  so let's move on to exhibit b  here we have some energy balls made with  peanut butter  rolled oats honey ground flaxseed  and raisins so yum energy balls are  another great example of a snack that  you can make easily  and inexpensively while also allowing  for some versatility depending on what  you have sitting in your pantry  so in this case we're getting healthy  fats and protein from the peanut butter  which  will also help to bind the energy balls  together with the fiber-rich oats i  also love the addition of raisins for  some natural sweetness which  are such an inexpensive pantry staple  and of course we've also got some  healthy fats from the flaxseed as well i  actually often make energy balls with my  son because  you really can't mess them up and  sometimes you know if  he adds too much of the dry ingredients  you could just bring it back with some  more nut butter or sweetener to kind of  like bind things together  also pro mom tip here folks put a few  chocolate chips or like sprinkles in  them  and they become a really hot commodity  we call them cookie balls in my house i  would say that if you want to up the  protein a bit or cut back on the  sugar since energy balls are typically  higher in sugar  hence the name energy balls you could  add some powdered peanut butter  or protein powder or just do a little  bit more  hemp or flaxseed and a little less oats  but yeah i love this snack last but not  least  let's take a look at exhibit c  so here we have banana strips with some  peanut butter some homemade vegan hot  fudge  chia seeds and some chocolate chips  my god okay so this snack is obviously a  little bit more  on the decking side and would totally be  a great  inexpensive dessert option so we're  getting some carbs and natural sweetness  from the banana  healthy fats and protein from the peanut  butter and chia  some extra fiber from the chia seeds and  we're bringing the satisfaction factor  with the chocolate and while in general  of course we are better off getting our  antioxidants from  whole fruits and vegetables if you want  another reason to enjoy dark chocolate  know that one study actually found that  cocoa and dark chocolate  did have more antioxidant activity than  any other fruit tested  even blueberries however it's important  to note that dark chocolate containing  a cocoa percentage of at least 70  percent or higher  will provide the most benefits while  also being relatively lower in sugar  but if you don't particularly like the  bitterness of dark chocolate on its own  i personally don't you could try melting  it down with a little bit of coconut oil  or mixing it into some peanut butter or  some  mashed ripe banana now if i was enjoying  this as a snack and not dessert after  a you know satiating meal i might want  to go for a little bit more protein in  there  so you could make a decadent mousse like  dip  by pureeing some silken tofu with the  chocolate  and the peanut butter i actually have a  recipe on my blog for this kind of like  peanut butter  protein mousse that i'll link to below  but that is a wrap  my friends again i want to thank  everyone who participated and submitted  their  delicious looking meals and snacks for  today's video  i hope that you are all feeling as  inspired as i am to make something  really tasty  out of all of these inexpensive and  accessible ingredients  don't forget to be following me on  instagram abby's kitchen to see the next  call out for submissions  and also a reminder to please be kind  and supportive in the comments  we don't want any food shaming going on  here  but if you like this video be sure to  give it the thumbs up leave me a comment  below with what theme i should be doing  next for these subscribe to the channel  and i'll see you next time on abby's  kitchen  bye
 

